IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `dg-core`

-- Delaware General Corporation Law, 8 Del. C. ch. 1: piece dg2 (ss 121 to 147) -- SMALL HELPERS SHARED BY THE dg2 MODULES.
--
-- Nothing here is law. Three-valued logic over MAYBE BOOLEAN, so that a vote that cannot be a vote
-- (the core's `the vote carries` answers NOTHING) is carried up and never turned into FALSE, and one test that
-- several sections of the piece make: whether a provision sits in the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws.
-- The source is the plain-text rendering de-code-t8-ch1-2026-10-01.txt (not the official text).

§ `Helpers`

-- Both findings must hold. FALSE as soon as one is FALSE; TRUE only if both are TRUE; otherwise not covered.
GIVEN a IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      b IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`dg2 both findings hold` a b MEANS
    CONSIDER a
    WHEN JUST x THEN (IF x THEN b ELSE JUST FALSE)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        CONSIDER b
        WHEN JUST y THEN (IF y THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST FALSE)
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

-- Either finding suffices. TRUE as soon as one is TRUE; FALSE only if both are FALSE; otherwise not covered.
GIVEN a IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      b IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`dg2 either finding holds` a b MEANS
    CONSIDER a
    WHEN JUST x THEN (IF x THEN JUST TRUE ELSE b)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        CONSIDER b
        WHEN JUST y THEN (IF y THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING)
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

-- A finding made certain: a BOOLEAN lifted into the three-valued form.
GIVEN a IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`dg2 the finding is certain` a MEANS JUST a

-- "unless the certificate of incorporation or bylaws otherwise provide", "unless otherwise restricted by the certificate of
-- incorporation or bylaws": only these two instruments count. A provision said to be made in a resolution of the board
-- of directors, or in none of these, is not one the text recognises in those places.
GIVEN w IS A `Where a provision is made`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`dg2 the place is the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws` w MEANS
    CONSIDER w
    WHEN `in the certificate of incorporation` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `in the bylaws` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE
